## Passes 3–5

**Pass 3 — Label probes:** 35 labels across every wing probed against `profile.npz` (cell 2.0 pt, 0.1954 m/cell) — Cotton, OTC, Vitamins, Laxatives, Hair Color, Toys, Batteries, Baby Wipes, Charcoal, Dry Dog Food, Sodas, Chips, Kitchen Gadget, Tortillas, Bread, Picante, Tobacco, Pastries, Juice, Diapers, Incontinence, Cosmetics, Seasonal, Foilware, Meat Snacks, Cereal — **35 OK / 0 MISS, all 0.00 m**. An independent sweep of all 229 in‑boundary page words found only two beyond 2 m: the `Bakery` and `Dairy` department titles, both printed inside blessed back‑of‑house rooms.

**Pass 4 — walk_truth adequacy:** every original point re‑probed and confirmed inside its named feature (not an adjacent frontage). Gaps found and closed under Finding 2.

**Pass 5 — Config sanity:** all four exclusions, four inclusions and five seal zones read and checked against the drawing. No inclusion blankets a staff room (the Produce/Seafood inclusion stops at `x=1184`, the wall band; the Deli inclusion stops at `x=1160` so the 7 pt staff gap stays sealed); no exclusion covers a shelf label's only frontage. The checkstand shape fix verified visually: 13 lanes sealed, the 25 pt front action alley open, aisles 12–19 running green to their south mouths.

**Cleared, not findings:** all 23 culled pockets classified (Dairy BOH 93.7 m², pharmacy dispensary 54.9 m², two service rooms, four restrooms, 13 checkout lanes, three wall‑case crevices); the pharmacy wing is fully green with the dispensary correctly sealed (no product label, two staff doors); Blooms, Meal Simple, Healthy Living, Market and Beer & Wine are all unanchored but fully green‑fronted; the aisle‑18 `H-E-B baby` logo pinches its corridor to 0.28 m capacity — the pixel‑frozen reference store 659 pinches to 0.24 m in eight aisles, so this is baseline pipeline behaviour, not a 227 defect.

**Note for maintainers (not a 227 blocker):** the short‑segment under‑sampling in `engine.build_grid` is a fleet‑wide risk — a drawn‑closed room can leak through any wall jog shorter than `2 × cell`. Store 227 is fully correct with data alone, so I did not touch code; worth a universal fix gated by the golden.

